# "Interrupts" — chaining a handler onto the front of the machine's own.
#
# Six characters go in — five letters and the Enter — and each one arrives as
# an interrupt, so the count at the end is six.
#
# On the machine's own console, which is the one the chapter shows and the one
# the frame beside it runs. Over a serial console the Kernal's echo path looks
# at the port while it sends, and a character that lands during the echo of the
# one before is taken without an interrupt — so the count there is three or
# four, and not the same twice. See ACCURACY A70.

console video
send HELLO\r
screen ^HELLO\s*$
screen ^THE PROCESSOR WAS INTERRUPTED 6 TIMES\s*$
